  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge Infrastructure for Food Systems in North Sumatra</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security is one of the national development priorities of Indonesia. Hence, the national government supports food production by developing Food Systems in specified strategic areas, among which is the Humbahas Food Estate regency in North Sumatra. The Dutch Government as well as private sector initiatives are interested to support these efforts, which include a knowledge-education component. Within the nexus of agrifood abd water and along the lines of the Dutch economic mission to the Food Estate area in North Sumatra (which took place in May 2022), the Netherlands &#x2013; as a leading country in the agriculture sector &#x2013; will bring in Dutch expertise to support local needs and to strengthen the learning system. The sustainability of food systems is also related to Climate Adaptation and the establishment of a Circular Agriculture. By means of Living Lab Sustainable Food Systems, as an innovative instrument to support business development in the Humbahas Food Estate regency and to become a sustainable food system, agricultural companies will be invited to submit a business case. These business cases (covering topics, such as circrcular agriculture, agricultural waste, agricultural storage and warehousing, commercial farming, and agritourism) will form the foundation for (digital) student projects executed by groups of students from Indonesia and the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
